  "lineage": "Japanese 20th-century sentimental popular-ballad genre derived from late-Meiji-period (1880s-1912) enka-shi street-political-protest-song tradition, transformed mid-Showa-period (1930s-1960s) into commercial recording-industry sentimental-vocal-pop. The vocal technique stresses kobushi melismatic-ornamental vibrato-and-microtonal-bend, koe-on chest-resonance projected-vocal, and pentatonic-yo minor-leaning melodic-vocabulary (often modulating through 4-cycle key changes per verse). Lyrical themes center on lost-love, distant-homeland, mother-and-rural-nostalgia, and ocean-and-port-imagery. The 1960s-1980s golden-age enka-orchestra featured strings-and-shamisen-and-shakuhachi hybrid-arrangement; 1990s-onward enka declined as a youth-genre but persists as a senior-audience-and-karaoke staple.",
